"""Photoreal Isaac-Sim hero render of the Conet Tactile inspection line.

Single source of truth for the marketing / handoff hero shots. Built from
``sim/specs.py`` (real dimensions) plus three on-disk authorities:

* the printable enclosure CAD at ``hardware/edge_enclosure/edge_enclosure.scad``
  → exported through OpenSCAD into STL → imported as a vertex-smoothed USD
  mesh so the chamfered bezel, the vent grille, the VESA pocket all read
  correctly (no hand-modelled stand-in cube).
* the procedural PBR texture set generated by ``sim.isaac.textures`` —
  concrete sweep, PU rubber belt, brushed anodized aluminium, polished
  stainless, Velostat fabric, green PCB solder mask, pharma white. Every
  big surface in the scene binds to one of those (diffuse + roughness +
  normal) so RTX path-traces real reflections / micro-shadows, not flat
  swatches.
* the factory HDRI at ``$SCENE_HDRI`` (default ``/workspace/hdri.hdr``).
  We add a **curved cyclorama** sweep behind everything so the polished
  concrete floor seamlessly bends up into the dome — no horizon line, no
  "floor stops here and HDRI starts" jump.

Geometry highlights:

* belt is one continuous loop that wraps around two end rollers
* rollers carry stainless end caps + bearing housings + a side drive motor
* frame is 40 mm T-slot aluminium extrusion (verticals, longitudinals,
  cross-braces, levelling feet)
* mesh sensor is a subdivided Velostat strip + a 10 mm cell grid + an FFC
  ribbon down to the scanner PCB
* the Tactile Edge kiosk is *only* the printed body+bezel from the .scad,
  with a recessed emissive 7" display and a detailed Jetson Orin Nano
  (finned heatsink + fan + GPIO header) sitting inside

Run on the GPU pod:

    OMNI_KIT_ACCEPT_EULA=YES python sim/isaac/scene.py

Outputs ``sim/isaac/out/twin_scene.png`` / ``twin_overview.png`` /
``twin_line.png`` (1600×1000, path-traced).
"""
